      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds okay, but to be honest the 'augmenting' thing is hard to sell when the main goal is reducing overhead. if i use AI to automate 30% of a department's tasks, i'm basically looking at having to cut staff to actually see the savings. is it just a standard business reality that automation eventually leads to downsizing, or is there a way to do it that isn't just calling it 'optimization' to hide layoffs?",
